  "answer": "Based on Statistics Canada Table 34-10-0063-01 (Capital expenditures, non-residential tangible assets, by type of asset and geography), the hydro-electric power plant capital expenditures for 2022 by province (in millions of current dollars) are:\n\n**2022:**\n- British Columbia: **2,742.0**\n- Quebec: 1,071.4\n- Ontario: 792.5\n- Manitoba: 302.2\n- Nova Scotia: 99.7\n- Newfoundland and Labrador: 42.2\n- Saskatchewan: 7.2\n- Others: suppressed or zero\n\n**2023:** Most provincial figures are suppressed (marked \"x\" or \"..\"), but Ontario reported 885.6, and the Canada total was 5,017.0.\n\n**2024 (for reference/trend):**\n- British Columbia: 1,908.6\n- Quebec: 1,251.9\n- Ontario: 791.3\n- Manitoba: 225.2\n\nBritish Columbia's 2022 expenditure alone (2,742.0 million) exceeds any other province's two-year total where data is available. The massive Site C Clean Energy Project ($16 billion, under construction 2015–2025) was in peak spending phase during 2022–2023, making BC the clear leader.\n\n**Answer: British Columbia** had the largest total capital expenditure in hydroelectric power generation over 2022–2023.",
